From 1a7020388b33a48e281d38b2f4a13877e3f3b696 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@e.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 05:48:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] port: bring Qwen3.6 feature work onto main's src/ stage
 layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ports the nine Qwen3.6 commits (vLLM migration, VRAM-aware model loading,
async I/O, two-pass table parsing, ticketing system) onto main's stage-based
src/ packages. A plain `git merge Qwen3.6` cannot do this: it hits a directory
rename split on core/ -> src/ and leaves api/ + src/api/ and core/ + src/core/
side by side, so this is a replay of the changes rather than a merge.

Generation backend (vLLM)
- src/config.py: VLLM_BASE_URL / VLLM_CHAT_URL / VLLM_CHAT_MODEL. Ollama
  settings are kept: the vision/ingestion path still uses them.
- stage_04_answer/generator_agent.py: httpx against the OpenAI-compatible
  /v1/chat/completions endpoint; generate() and generate_stream() are async.
  The Ollama model-fallback list is dropped (vLLM serves one model) and
  replaced with logged errors.
- Async propagated through RAGChatbotEngine.process_query, RAGChatbot,
  KnowledgeRetriever, the FastAPI chat/search routes, the main.py CLI, and
  the affected tests (asyncio.run, so no pytest-asyncio dependency).

VRAM-aware model placement
- src/core/gpu_utils.py: pick_device(min_free_gb).
- MIN_VRAM_GB_EMBEDDER / _RERANKER / _REWRITER in config.
- Applied to BGEM3Embedder and, since main replaced the LLM dialect rewriter
  with AraT5, to AraT5DialectRewriter (the Qwen3.6 reranker_agent change has
  no target: main's PriorityReranker loads no cross-encoder).

Two-pass table-aware vision parsing
- ENABLE_TABLE_ROUTING / SAVE_TABLE_DEBUG_IMAGES / MAX_TABLES_PER_PAGE and
  TABLE_VISION_PROMPT in config.
- ingestion.py: _single_pass_page, _save_table_debug_image, _stitch_tables,
  and a rewritten process_vision_page.
- verify_table_routing.py moved under src/kb_ingestor/ (main has no scripts/).

Ticketing (stage_05_ticket)
- New src/pipeline/stage_05_ticket/ package holding TicketIntakeAgent and the
  two prompts, replacing the graph.py node it lived in on Qwen3.6.
- TicketRegistry added to src/cache_db/document_registry.py.
- Intake runs as stage 0 of process_query and answer_question_stream, before
  cache and retrieval, since neither trigger needs the knowledge base.
  process_query and the wrapper now thread `history` through, which the
  stateless contact-collection exchange requires.
- Admin ticket endpoints + tickets tab in the admin panel.
- Low-confidence dead ends now return PROMPT_LOW_CONFIDENCE (offer to
  escalate) instead of a flat "no information found".
- The escalation prompt is never cached: it is conversational state, not an
  answer. Multi-turn requests also no longer read or write the single-turn
  semantic cache.

Observability
- api/main.py configures the root logger so INFO app logs surface under
  uvicorn. Qwen3.6's per-stage _log_timings is not ported: main's
  PipelineProfiler already records per-stage latency, and ticket_intake is
  registered as a profiler stage.

Deliberate main-side wins: RELEVANCE_THRESHOLD stays at main's 40 (Qwen3.6
still had the old 50), and the src/ layout, stage packages, monitoring, and
tests are untouched.

One behavioural fix beyond a straight port, marked in the source:
_ENGINEER_NO_RE now tolerates a definite article, so "الرقم النقابي" -- the
exact wording PROMPT_USER_INTENT asks the user for -- parses. Previously only
the bare "رقم نقابي" matched and the engineer number was silently dropped
from every ticket.
